WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.886 --> 00:00:21.233
Fantine arrived at the door of Mayor Madeleine's factory and was promptly hired.

2
00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:25.480
She had no experience in making jewelry, so she worked slowly.

3
00:00:25.481 --> 00:00:30.893
As a result, she did not receive much money for each day's work, but it was enough.

4
00:00:30.894 --> 00:00:34.738
Fantine thought only of Cosette and their future together.

5
00:00:34.739 --> 00:00:39.877
Because Fantine wasn't married, she was careful never to mention her little girl to anyone.

6
00:00:39.878 --> 00:00:44.206
She rented a small room and borrowed money to buy furniture for it.

7
00:00:44.207 --> 00:00:48.798
Fantine was earning her own living, and she was almost happy.

8
00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:53.869
Meanwhile, thanks to Fantine, Monsieur Thenardier had been able to pay his debt.

9
00:00:53.870 --> 00:01:01.448
Within a month the family needed more money, so Madame Thenardier took Cosette's clothes to Paris, where she sold them.

10
00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:05.853
When this money ran out, the Thenardiers began to resent Cosette.

11
00:01:05.854 --> 00:01:12.758
They dressed her in rags and fed her leftovers. She ate under the table with the dog and the cat.

12
00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:18.416
Since Fantine could not read or write, she hired a man to write her letters for her.

13
00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:26.321
She wrote twice a month to the Thenardiers. Their reply was always the same: Cosette is doing wonderfully well.

14
00:01:26.322 --> 00:01:32.213
After a year Monsieur Thenardier demanded that Fantine pay 12 francs a month instead of 7.

15
00:01:32.214 --> 00:01:37.498
Fantine gladly sent the money because she thought Cosette was being well cared for.

16
00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:45.046
In reality Madame Thenardier loved her own daughters, Eponine and Azelma, and hated Cosette.

17
00:01:45.047 --> 00:01:49.902
Seeing their mother treating Cosette cruelly, the two girls did the same.

18
00:01:49.903 --> 00:01:54.919
Meanwhile people in Fantine's hometown watched her and gossiped about her.

19
00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:00.229
More than one person was envious of her thick blond hair and fine white teeth.

20
00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:05.245
It became common knowledge that she wrote regularly to the innkeeper in Montfermeil.

21
00:02:05.246 --> 00:02:11.800
The man who wrote her letters could not keep a secret; he was the one who revealed that she had a child.

22
00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:16.793
An old woman who liked to gossip wanted to find out for herself what was going on.

23
00:02:16.794 --> 00:02:22.716
She traveled to Montfermeil, talked to the Thenardiers, and actually saw Cosette.

24
00:02:22.717 --> 00:02:31.295
Monsieur Thenardier decided to demand 15 francs a month from Fantine. Somehow the young woman managed to make the payments.

25
00:02:31.296 --> 00:02:37.779
But soon after the old woman returned from Montfermeil, Fantine was summoned by the factory supervisor.

26
00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:43.866
This supervisor told Fantine that she was no longer employed and handed her fifty francs.

27
00:02:43.867 --> 00:02:48.684
The supervisor also told her that the mayor had suggested that she leave the city.

28
00:02:48.685 --> 00:02:56.350
Fantine was shocked. "I cannot leave the city," she thought. "I am in debt for my rent and my furniture."

29
00:02:56.351 --> 00:03:04.850
Fifty francs wasn't enough to pay her debts, never mind transportation. Ashamed and distraught, Fantine slipped away to her room.

30
00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:11.509
After that, it did not take long for Fantine to fall behind on her payments to the Thenardiers.

31
00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:19.834
Two more years passed. If Fantine had been able to return to Montfermeil, she would not have recognized her child.

32
00:03:19.835 --> 00:03:27.818
Cosette, so fresh and pretty when she'd arrived at the inn, was now thin and pale. Cruelty had made her ugly.

33
00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:36.326
Her large blue eyes were filled with sadness. She was a miserable sight to see in the winter, sweeping the sidewalk before daybreak.

34
00:03:36.327 --> 00:03:43.818
Everyone called her the Lark because she was like a tiny, busy bird. Only this poor lark never sang.

35
00:03:43.819 --> 00:03:50.810
What had become of Fantine? When she was fired from the factory, she thought that she would get a job as a servant.

36
00:03:50.811 --> 00:03:54.635
She went from one house to another, but nobody wanted her.

37
00:03:54.636 --> 00:04:00.532
The furniture dealer to whom she owed money said, "If you leave the city, I'll have you arrested as a thief!"

38
00:04:00.533 --> 00:04:08.707
Her landlord also threatened her. So Fantine divided the little money she had between the furniture dealer and the landlord.

39
00:04:08.708 --> 00:04:14.699
It still was not enough. She began to make shirts for the soldiers at the local garrison.

40
00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:24.024
She earned 12 sous a day; Cosette was costing her 10 sous. She lived as cheaply as she could, doing without heat or even a candle.

41
00:04:24.025 --> 00:04:30.763
Her clothes became more and more ragged. Fantine had one friend: her neighbor Marguerite.

42
00:04:30.764 --> 00:04:37.533
"If I sleep only five hours a night and work the rest of the time, I might have enough money," she told Marguerite.

43
00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:40.526
But over time Fantine became exhausted.

44
00:04:40.527 --> 00:04:47.755
The slight cough she had grew worse. Sometimes she said to Marguerite, "Just feel how hot my hands are."

45
00:04:47.756 --> 00:04:53.342
One day the Thenardiers wrote to Fantine and said that Cosette didn't have any winter clothes.

46
00:04:53.343 --> 00:04:57.413
They said that Fantine must send at least ten francs for a wool skirt.

47
00:04:57.414 --> 00:05:03.231
All day Fantine worried about what to do. That evening she went to the barbershop.

48
00:05:03.232 --> 00:05:11.152
"What beautiful hair!" said the barber when Fantine removed the combs from her head. Her hair hung down to her waist.

49
00:05:11.153 --> 00:05:15.985
"How much will you give me for it? I understand there's a demand for hair for wigs."

50
00:05:15.986 --> 00:05:17.455
"Ten francs."

51
00:05:17.456 --> 00:05:21.406
"Then cut it all off," she said quickly before she could change her mind.

52
00:05:21.407 --> 00:05:26.969
Fantine bought a knit skirt and sent it to the Thenardiers. They were furious.

53
00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:34.874
They had wanted the money, not the skirt, so they gave the skirt to Eponine. Cosette still shivered, but Fantine was happy.

54
00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:42.477
"My child is no longer cold," she told Marguerite. "I have clothed her with my hair." She didn't know the truth.

55
00:05:42.478 --> 00:05:48.731
Fantine put on a little round cap to conceal her short hair and somehow still managed to look pretty.

56
00:05:48.732 --> 00:05:53.041
But she felt sad that she had had to cut her beautiful hair.

57
00:05:53.042 --> 00:05:58.945
Every time she passed the factory, she resented Mayor Madeleine and blamed him for her troubles.

58
00:05:58.946 --> 00:06:06.929
Soon she received another letter from the Thenardiers. Cosette was seriously ill with a fever and her medicine was expensive.

59
00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:13.270
"Unless you send us forty francs," wrote Monsieur Thenardier, "your daughter will surely die."

60
00:06:13.271 --> 00:06:19.096
"Forty francs! Where will I get that kind of money?" Fantine asked Marguerite.

61
00:06:19.097 --> 00:06:25.683
But that very day, she noticed a traveling dentist in the square, and he noticed her beautiful white teeth.

62
00:06:25.684 --> 00:06:33.675
"If you will sell me two of your front teeth," said the dentist, "I'll pay you well. Your teeth will make wonderful false teeth."

63
00:06:33.676 --> 00:06:36.514
"Don't be ridiculous!" said Fantine.

64
00:06:36.515 --> 00:06:41.159
"How much money did he offer?" asked Marguerite, when Fantine told her the story.

65
00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:43.137
"Twenty francs per tooth."

66
00:06:43.138 --> 00:06:47.080
"That's forty francs," said Marguerite.

67
00:06:47.081 --> 00:06:50.180
"I know," said Fantine quietly.

68
00:06:50.181 --> 00:06:55.144
"Have you ever heard of this kind of fever?" She showed the Thenardiers' letter to Marguerite.

69
00:06:55.144 --> 00:06:59.405
"Does it attack children? Do people really die from it?"

70
00:06:59.406 --> 00:07:03.970
"Yes, people die, especially children," said Marguerite.

71
00:07:03.971 --> 00:07:10.628
Later that night Fantine went in search of the dentist. She sent the forty francs to the Thenardiers right away.

72
00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:18.707
Poor Fantine! She didn't know that Cosette wasn't really sick. It was all a trick for the Thenardiers to get more money from her.

73
00:07:18.708 --> 00:07:25.620
Fantine coughed while she sewed the soldiers' shirts. She was coughing when she read Monsieur Thenardier's next letter.

74
00:07:25.621 --> 00:07:33.043
"Cosette is still recovering," he wrote. "I must have one hundred francs immediately or I will have to turn her out into the street."

75
00:07:33.044 --> 00:07:37.100
"What will I do?" cried Fantine.
